# {{PRODUCT}} — Claude Code

**Source of truth:** `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` (and `AGENTS.md`).

## Reviewers

Run only the reviewer roles selected by `.agents/scripts/review_policy.py` against the same immutable review package. Agent files are generated under `.claude/agents/`. Reviewers must be invoked as independent subagents; the lead agent is strictly forbidden from self-certifying reviews or using `record_review.py --verdict PASS` on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes. Missing required coverage or malformed output blocks delivery.

On-demand specialists (`.claude/agents/`):
- `qa-diagnostics-agent` (Logcat crash forensics)
- `android-ui-expert-agent` (Compose & RTL)
- `test-quality-reviewer-agent` (Unit & UI test quality audits)

Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}}
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough: After every device installation (`run_device.py install-start`), the agent MUST output a complete, numbered mobile verification walkthrough (Navigation path, Preconditions, User actions, Expected results, Edge cases) in chat BEFORE asking the developer for sign-off. Never ask if it passed without detailing how to navigate to and test the specific modified feature.
- Zero-Polling Invariant: Never poll background tasks or subagents in a loop. Yield execution and wait for subagent completion messages.
- Review Ingestion & Harvesting: Ingest reviewer responses with `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --from-subagent <role>=<convId>` or directly with `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --response-text "<name>=<text>"`. Clean reviews with `cites=0` and explanatory prose are recognized as `PASS`.
- Task Resumption: If a task becomes BLOCKED or fixes are needed, run `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py resume --repo . --task-id <id>` to return to implementation.

{{GIT_POLICY}}

Read `ENFORCEMENT_TIER` and `ENFORCEMENT_BY_HOST` from `.agents/scripts/_product.py`. Claude's executable hook may hard-enforce covered mutations, but conversational approval remains `RULE_ENFORCED`; never claim cryptographic human separation.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Canonical Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/project_graph.py --feature <name>` (or `--find <Symbol>`) | Fast AST/symbol project graph analysis |
| **Clarification** | Interactive question with developer before drafting plan |
| **Context Note** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<note>"` | Record architectural convention/note |
| **Preflight Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/preflight.py` (or `preflight_check.py`) | Deterministic check: room, fast ktlint, string parity |
| **Unit Tests** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_tests_gate.py` | Run unit tests gate |
| **Review Package** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/review_package.py` | Generate immutable review package markdown |
| **Review Harvest** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --from-subagent <role>=<convId>` | Auto-harvest subagent transcript and record review |
| **Review Text** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/record_review.py --task <id> --response-text "<role>=<text>"` | Direct review text ingestion with evidence footer |
| **Resume Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py resume --repo . --task-id <id>` | Resume task from BLOCKED or VERIFYING back to implementation |
| **Assemble Debug** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_gradle_task.py {{ASSEMBLE}}` | Diagnostic assemble is allowed in IMPLEMENTING; final delivery assemble requires all reviewers PASS |
| **Device Deploy** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/run_device.py install-start` | Install and launch on target device/emulator |
| **Screen Capture** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/capture_screen.py --output-name <name>` | Capture device screen for verification proof |
| **Final Verify** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py verify --repo . --task-id <id>` | Read-only delivery verification check |
| **Deliver Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/scripts/workflow.py deliver --repo . --task-id <id>` | Finalize delivery state after git commit |
